Restore the web client's last active workspace after a restart

After a workspace restart the tile lands on Landing - "Select a workspace from
the sidebar to begin" - even though the sidebar lists every worktree. Upstream's
paired-client session read already restores this from `ui.lastActiveRepoId` and
`ui.lastActiveWorktreeId`, but nothing anywhere writes those two fields: the
producer was never implemented, on desktop or on web, so the boot session is
empty and Landing renders.

`rememberWebActiveWorkspace` records the pointer from the web session adapter
through the existing `ui.set` RPC, which persists into the host's own `ui` slice
- so a browser with empty storage, or a different browser entirely, still
restores. Only the `local` partition is read, the write is memoized so it fires
on change rather than on every session write, and a failed RPC drops the memo so
the next write retries. `getStoredWorkspaceSession` falls back to the browser's
sanitized copy when the host pointer is absent.

The pointer is built from the keys the caller actually sent. One of the four
call sites is `session.patch`, which passes a raw `Partial`, so coercing an
absent key to null would clear the other half - switching worktree would erase
the repo id, and the restore's `ui.lastActiveRepoId ?? localSession.activeRepoId`
fallback cannot fall through a stored null, only an absent one. The unchanged
half is carried forward from the memo, or from browser storage when the memo has
been dropped.

The browser copy is written before the active-environment check on purpose: it
is this client's own UI state, and a client that is not currently paired should
still reopen where it left off.

To test, open a worktree in the tile, restart the workspace, and reload: that
worktree should be active. Switch worktrees within a repo and reload again - the
repo must not be lost. Repeat in a browser with cleared storage. Covered by
`web-preload-api.test.ts` and
`web-preload-api-active-workspace-pointer.test.ts`.
